{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-77526-r4518962","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Kuddi (Spiced Yogurt Sauce)","sourcePageId":77526,"sourceRevision":"4518962","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:19:27Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Kuddi%20(Spiced%20Yogurt%20Sauce)&oldid=4518962","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:15.213Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Low-GI recipes","Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using chickpea flour","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1fbb4fa7657c779c052279cd91a8d7733ab8adf365ad20eabebf4f373f7aef88","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| Category = Indian recipes\n| Time = 15 minutes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Rating = 2\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Cuisine of India]]\n\n'''Kuddi''', also called '''kadhi''', is a sort of gravy based on yogurt and chickpea flour. It can be served with pakora, rice, or roti.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*½ [[Cookbook:Liter|litre]] (1 [[Cookbook:Pint|pint]]) [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yoghurt]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Chickpea Flour|besan]] (Indian chickpea flour)\n*2–3 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] piece of fresh [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]], grated\n*1 [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|green chilli]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cumin|jeera seeds]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine the yogurt, chickpea flour, sugar, salt, grated ginger, and chopped green chilli.\n#Heat and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] with continuous stirring.\n#Taste and add more sugar or salt as needed. It should be sour, salty, and sweet.\n#[[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] the jeera seeds in butter, and mix them into the kuddi.\n#Serve.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Low-GI recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Kuddi (Spiced Yogurt Sauce)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ litre (1 pint) yoghurt","sourceText":"½ litre (1 pint) yoghurt","amountText":"½ litre (1 pint) yoghurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 teaspoon besan (Indian chickpea flour)","sourceText":"1 teaspoon besan (Indian chickpea flour)","amountText":"1 teaspoon besan (Indian chickpea